<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Varna Ratnakara</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">14th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/varna">Varna</a> Ratnakara is a Maithili prose work written by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jyotirishvara-thakur">Jyotirishvara Thakur</a> at the Karnat court of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mithila">Mithila</a> in the early 14th century. It is a manual of descriptions for poets and storytellers, covering cities, courts, seasons, people and crafts. It is among the earliest surviving prose works in Maithili and a rich source for medieval north Indian life.</p></div>
